@@ -3,11 +3,45 @@
 Terraform for the reports bucket and the key the nightly export job uploads with. The job reads
 the key from `terraform output`.
 
-## Usage
+State is stored in S3 (versioned, KMS-encrypted, public access blocked, TLS-only, native
+lockfile locking via `use_lockfile`, so no DynamoDB table). Requires Terraform >= 1.10.
+**The state contains the uploader's secret access key**, so limit who can read the bucket and
+the KMS key `alias/reports-tfstate` to people who may see that key.
+
+## One-time bootstrap (one person, once)
+
+The state bucket is created by `bootstrap/`, which keeps its own state locally (it can't
+store state in a bucket that doesn't exist yet). It only holds the bucket and KMS key, no secrets.
+
+```sh
+cd bootstrap
+terraform init
+terraform apply
+```
+
+Then set the bucket name in `backend.tf` (default `reports-tfstate-<account id>`; see
+`terraform output bucket`) and commit. Keep `bootstrap/terraform.tfstate` somewhere safe
+(it is gitignored); the bucket has `prevent_destroy`.
+
+## Migrating the existing local state (once)
+
+From the laptop that has the current `terraform.tfstate`:
+
+```sh
+terraform init -migrate-state   # answer "yes" to copy local state to S3
+terraform plan                  # should show no changes
+```
+
+After verifying, delete the local `terraform.tfstate*` files.
+
+## Daily workflow (everyone)
+
+Needs AWS credentials with access to the state bucket and KMS key.
 
 ```sh
 terraform init
+terraform plan
 terraform apply
 ```
 
-State is kept locally in `terraform.tfstate`, so only the person who last ran `apply` has it.
+Locking prevents concurrent applies. If a run crashes, use `terraform force-unlock <id>`.
diff --git a/backend.tf b/backend.tf
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fd24681
--- /dev/null
+++ b/backend.tf
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# Bucket is created by ./bootstrap. Backend blocks cannot use variables, so replace
+# <ACCOUNT_ID> with the AWS account id (or pass -backend-config at init).
+terraform {
+  backend "s3" {
+    bucket       = "reports-tfstate-<ACCOUNT_ID>"
+    key          = "reports/terraform.tfstate"
+    region       = "eu-north-1"
+    encrypt      = true
+    kms_key_id   = "alias/reports-tfstate"
+    use_lockfile = true
+  }
+}
